## Tooling

- **Serena** — the project is semantically indexed. Mandatory to use it to locate functions, logic, variables, and code symbols. Work fastest-first (`get_symbols_overview` → `find_symbol` → `read_file`), and use `search_for_pattern` in place of grep; see [Need for speed](#need-for-speed). If Serena is unavailable, say so in one line and fall back to a scoped pattern search — do not spend turns installing or restarting it. If you run `serena project health-check`, set `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8` first, or its Windows console encoding makes a passing check look like a failure. **Run `serena project index` strictly during `/project-checkpoint` milestones or when creating new packages. Never run it during iterative code edits or quick bugfixes.**
- **Graphify** — structural knowledge graph in `graphify-out/`. Use `graphify query|path|explain`
  to understand architecture before editing. **Run `graphify update .` strictly during `/project-checkpoint` milestones or when creating new packages. Never run it during iterative code edits or quick bugfixes.**

